    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250-a2">

                <pb facs="0346" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg272"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. de Lhuys to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 8, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: You have had the kindness to communicate to
                    me the proclamation by which President Johnson has definitely given his official
                    sanction to the amendment to the Constitution of the United States relative to
                    the abolition of slavery over the whole extent of the federal territory.</p>
                <p>You have justly thought, sir, that neither the government of the Emperor nor
                    public opinion could view with indifference a measure destined to ameliorate the
                    moral and material condition of several millions of human beings. We ourselves,
                    several years ago, took the initiative in the suppression of slavery in our
                    colonies. We, therefore, cannot but applaud the generous sentiment which has
                    suggested to your government a measure so in harmony with the general progress
                    of humanity.</p>
                <p>Accept the assurances of the high consideration with which I have the honor to
                    be, sir, your very humble and very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>DROUYN DE LHUYS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bigelow</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Minister of the United States at Paris.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
